Description: Provides two flexible neo-normal probability distributions,
    MSNBurr and MSNBurr-IIa, as user-defined distributions for the 'NIMBLE'
    Bayesian inference framework. Both distributions extend the normal
    distribution with a shape parameter controlling skewness. The package
    provides density, distribution, quantile, and random generation
    functions for use in 'NIMBLE' models, with derivative support for
    Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (HMC) and No-U-Turn Sampler (NUTS) methods,
    and helpers that follow the Bayesian workflow: prior and posterior
    predictive simulation, dispersed initial values, convergence
    diagnostics (rank-normalised R-hat and effective sample size) and WAIC.
